{"part":2,"of":2,"expected_rows_in_part":23,"rows":[{"id":"TR-024","input":"parce que","type":"conjunction","gender":"","english":"because","notes":"Elides to parce qu' before a vowel: parce qu'il pleut.","example_fr":"Je reste parce qu'il pleut.","example_en":"I'm staying because it's raining.","engine_action":"verify-existing","status":"reference-pending","sources":[],"teacher_review":"not required (owner decision)"},{"id":"TR-025","input":"vieux","type":"adjective","gender":"","english":"old","notes":"vieux (m.s.), vieil (m.s. before vowel or mute h), vieille (f.s.), vieux (m.pl.), vieilles (f.pl.).","example_fr":"Un vieil homme.","example_en":"An old man.","engine_action":"add-missing","status":"source-verified","sources":["https://edtechbooks.org/docx/7717"],"teacher_review":"not required (owner decision)"},{"id":"TR-026","input":"mort","type":"adjective / noun","gender":"m. / f.","english":"dead; death","notes":"Adjective and past participle of mourir: il est mort, elle est morte. Nouns: la mort (death, f.), un mort (dead person, m.).","example_fr":"Il est mort hier.","example_en":"He died yesterday.","engine_action":"add-missing","status":"reference-pending","sources":[],"teacher_review":"not required (owner decision)"},{"id":"TR-027","input":"oeil","type":"noun","gender":"m.","english":"eye","notes":"Standard spelling is œil with the ligature; plural yeux. Compounds keep the regular plural: des œils-de-bœuf. Unligatured oeil is a common typed variant and should be accepted as input.","example_fr":"Elle a les yeux bleus.","example_en":"She has blue eyes.","engine_action":"add-missing","status":"source-verified","sources":["https://vitrinelinguistique.oqlf.gouv.qc.ca/21611/lorthographe/problemes-lies-aux-voyelles/ecriture-et-prononciation-des-lettres-doubles-ae-et-oe","https://kaweah.freedombox.rocks/kiwix/wiktionary_en_all_maxi_2023-04/oeil","https://www.synonyme-du-mot.com/les-articles/comment-dit-on-un-buf-au-pluriel"],"teacher_review":"not required (owner decision)"},{"id":"TR-028","input":"homme","type":"noun","gender":"m.","english":"man","notes":"Mute h: l'homme, un homme. Plural hommes.","example_fr":"Cet homme est gentil.","example_en":"This man is kind.","engine_action":"verify-existing","status":"reference-pending","sources":[],"teacher_review":"not required (owner decision)"},{"id":"TR-029","input":"heure","type":"noun","gender":"f.","english":"hour; time","notes":"Mute h: l'heure. Time telling: Quelle heure est-il ? À l'heure = on time.","example_fr":"Il est trois heures.","example_en":"It is three o'clock.","engine_action":"add-missing","status":"reference-pending","sources":[],"teacher_review":"not required (owner decision)"},{"id":"TR-030","input":"an","type":"noun","gender":"m.","english":"year","notes":"Counts years: j'ai vingt ans, par an, l'an dernier. Compare année, which stresses duration.","example_fr":"J'ai vingt ans.","example_en":"I am twenty.","engine_action":"add-missing","status":"reference-pending","sources":[],"teacher_review":"not required (owner decision)"},{"id":"TR-031","input":"enfant","type":"noun","gender":"m. / f.","english":"child","notes":"Same form for both genders: un enfant, une enfant. Plural enfants.","example_fr":"Les enfants jouent.","example_en":"The children are playing.","engine_action":"verify-existing","status":"reference-pending","sources":[],"teacher_review":"not required (owner decision)"},{"id":"TR-032","input":"air","type":"noun","gender":"m.","english":"air; look, tune","notes":"un air. Idioms: en plein air (outdoors), avoir l'air (to seem).","example_fr":"Il a l'air fatigué.","example_en":"He looks tired.","engine_action":"add-missing","status":"reference-pending","sources":[],"teacher_review":"not required (owner decision)"},{"id":"TR-033","input":"ami","type":"noun","gender":"m.","english":"friend","notes":"Feminine amie. petit ami / petite amie = boyfriend / girlfriend.","example_fr":"C'est mon ami.","example_en":"He is my friend.","engine_action":"verify-existing","status":"reference-pending","sources":[],"teacher_review":"not required (owner decision)"},{"id":"TR-034","input":"gens","type":"noun (plural only)","gender":"m. pl.","english":"people","notes":"No singular. A feminine adjective placed immediately before gens agrees in the feminine (les vieilles gens, les bonnes gens, toutes les vieilles gens); an adjective after gens is masculine (des gens intéressants). Jeunes gens is always masculine.","example_fr":"Les vieilles gens sont prudents.","example_en":"Old people are careful.","engine_action":"add-missing","status":"source-verified","sources":["https://dictionnaire-academie.fr/article/A9G0532","https://vitrinelinguistique.oqlf.gouv.qc.ca/23428/la-grammaire/le-nom/genre-des-noms/genre-du-nom-gens"],"teacher_review":"not required (owner decision)"},{"id":"TR-035","input":"accord","type":"noun","gender":"m.","english":"agreement; chord; consent","notes":"d'accord = OK. Grammar: l'accord du verbe (verb agreement).","example_fr":"Je suis d'accord.","example_en":"I agree.","engine_action":"add-missing","status":"reference-pending","sources":[],"teacher_review":"not required (owner decision)"},{"id":"TR-036","input":"amour","type":"noun","gender":"m.","english":"love","notes":"Masculine singular. In literary use the plural can be feminine: de belles amours.","example_fr":"Un grand amour.","example_en":"A great love.","engine_action":"verify-existing","status":"reference-pending","sources":[],"teacher_review":"not required (owner decision)"},{"id":"TR-037","input":"eau","type":"noun","gender":"f.","english":"water","notes":"Plural eaux. Mute elision: l'eau.","example_fr":"Un verre d'eau.","example_en":"A glass of water.","engine_action":"verify-existing","status":"reference-pending","sources":[],"teacher_review":"not required (owner decision)"},{"id":"TR-038","input":"histoire","type":"noun","gender":"f.","english":"history; story","notes":"l'histoire de France, raconter une histoire.","example_fr":"Elle raconte une histoire.","example_en":"She tells a story.","engine_action":"add-missing","status":"reference-pending","sources":[],"teacher_review":"not required (owner decision)"},{"id":"TR-039","input":"idée","type":"noun","gender":"f.","english":"idea","notes":"J'ai une idée. Plural idées.","example_fr":"J'ai une bonne idée.","example_en":"I have a good idea.","engine_action":"add-missing","status":"reference-pending","sources":[],"teacher_review":"not required (owner decision)"},{"id":"TR-040","input":"argent","type":"noun","gender":"m.","english":"money; silver","notes":"Uncountable for money: de l'argent, pas d'argent.","example_fr":"Je n'ai pas d'argent.","example_en":"I have no money.","engine_action":"add-missing","status":"reference-pending","sources":[],"teacher_review":"not required (owner decision)"},{"id":"TR-041","input":"année","type":"noun","gender":"f.","english":"year","notes":"Stresses the span of a year: toute l'année, bonne année. Compare an.","example_fr":"Bonne année !","example_en":"Happy New Year!","engine_action":"add-missing","status":"reference-pending","sources":[],"teacher_review":"not required (owner decision)"},{"id":"TR-042","input":"affaire","type":"noun","gender":"f.","english":"matter, deal, business","notes":"une bonne affaire (a bargain), les affaires (business, belongings), avoir affaire à (to deal with).","example_fr":"C'est une bonne affaire.","example_en":"It's a bargain.","engine_action":"add-missing","status":"reference-pending","sources":[],"teacher_review":"not required (owner decision)"},{"id":"TR-043","input":"coeur","type":"noun","gender":"m.","english":"heart","notes":"Standard spelling is cœur with the ligature; unligatured coeur is a tolerated variant in less formal writing. Idioms: par cœur (by heart), avoir mal au cœur (feel sick), un coup de cœur (a favourite).","example_fr":"Il a bon cœur.","example_en":"He has a good heart.","engine_action":"add-missing","status":"source-verified","sources":["https://vitrinelinguistique.oqlf.gouv.qc.ca/21611/lorthographe/problemes-lies-aux-voyelles/ecriture-et-prononciation-des-lettres-doubles-ae-et-oe","https://www.laculturegenerale.com/coup-de-coeur-ou-coups-de-coeur-pluriel-orthographe-exemples-faq/"],"teacher_review":"not required (owner decision)"},{"id":"TR-044","input":"bras","type":"noun","gender":"m.","english":"arm","notes":"Same form in singular and plural.","example_fr":"Elle porte l'enfant dans ses bras.","example_en":"She carries the child in her arms.","engine_action":"add-missing","status":"reference-pending","sources":[],"teacher_review":"not required (owner decision)"},{"id":"TR-045","input":"apprendre","type":"verb (irregular)","gender":"","english":"to learn; to teach","notes":"Conjugates like prendre: j'apprends, tu apprends, il apprend, nous apprenons, vous apprenez, ils apprennent; participle appris. apprendre à + infinitive.","example_fr":"J'apprends à nager.","example_en":"I am learning to swim.","engine_action":"verify-existing","status":"reference-pending","sources":[],"teacher_review":"not required (owner decision)"},{"id":"TR-046","input":"noir","type":"adjective / noun","gender":"m.","english":"black; darkness","notes":"noir, noire, noirs, noires. Noun: le noir (the dark).","example_fr":"Un chat noir.","example_en":"A black cat.","engine_action":"add-missing","status":"reference-pending","sources":[],"teacher_review":"not required (owner decision)"}],"proposed_rules":[{"id":"NR-01","topic":"oe/œ lookup normalization","rule":"Match oeil/coeur/soeur/oeuf/noeud/voeu/boeuf/oeuvre/moeurs/manoeuvre/choeur to their ligature forms by an explicit whitelist only. Never blanket-replace oe: coexister, coexistence and similar words must stay unligatured.","positive":["oeil -> œil","coeur -> cœur"],"negative":["coexister (do not change)"],"sources":["https://vitrinelinguistique.oqlf.gouv.qc.ca/21611/lorthographe/problemes-lies-aux-voyelles/ecriture-et-prononciation-des-lettres-doubles-ae-et-oe"]},{"id":"NR-02","topic":"gens agreement","rule":"A feminine-capable adjective immediately before gens is feminine; one after gens is masculine; tout/quel before it follow the feminine (toutes les vieilles gens). Jeunes gens is masculine. Report as a note, not an error, because the Académie describes a rule with tolerated variation.","positive":["les vieilles gens","des gens intéressants"],"negative":["des gens intéressantes -> flag"],"sources":["https://dictionnaire-academie.fr/article/A9G0532","https://vitrinelinguistique.oqlf.gouv.qc.ca/23428/la-grammaire/le-nom/genre-des-noms/genre-du-nom-gens"]},{"id":"NR-03","topic":"leur vs leurs","rule":"Before a verb, leur is the invariable pronoun: flag 'leurs' directly before a verb. Before a noun, leur/leurs agrees with the noun.","positive":["Je leur ai dit.","leurs enfants","leur maison"],"negative":["*Je leurs ai dit -> Je leur ai dit"],"sources":["https://vitrinelinguistique.oqlf.gouv.qc.ca/22360/la-grammaire/les-homophones-grammaticaux/les-homophones-leur-et-leurs"]},{"id":"NR-04","topic":"tout adverb agreement","rule":"Adverb tout is invariable, except before a feminine adjective beginning with a consonne or aspirated h, where it agrees (toute contente, toutes seules). Before a vowel it stays tout (tout heureuse).","positive":["Elle est toute contente.","Ils sont tout contents.","Elle est tout heureuse."],"negative":["*Elle est tout contente -> toute contente"],"sources":["https://cahier-francais.lerobert.com/9782321012870/asset/5b5b0643cb223.pdf","https://nos-langues.canada.ca/fr/cles-de-la-redaction/tout-accord-de-ladverbe"]},{"id":"NR-05","topic":"beau/vieux liaison forms","rule":"Before a masculine singular noun starting with a vowel or mute h use bel/vieil.","positive":["un bel arbre","un vieil homme"],"negative":["*un beau arbre","*un vieux homme"],"sources":["https://edtechbooks.org/docx/7717"]},{"id":"NR-06","topic":"si elision","rule":"si elides only before il/ils (s'il, s'ils). Never s'elle.","positive":["s'il pleut","si elle vient"],"negative":["*s'elle vient"],"sources":[]}]}
